<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Promises, Promises</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œWell a wife, or a husband, is when two people who are in love decide to dedicate themselves to each other for the rest of their lives, it's like a-â€&lt;br /&gt;â€œ- Like a promise?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He smiles, â€œYeah, itâ€™s a promise to love each other forever. Thereâ€™s a whole ceremony where itâ€™s made official, letting everyone know that theyâ€™ve chosen each other.â€&lt;br /&gt;Catra smiles, it sounds nice. Sounds similar to a promise she and Adora had made so many years ago, but theirs held none of the permanence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Series of one shots about promises in their relationship. Almost all of it is from Catra's POV.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Edit completed 12/08/2021 (08/12/2021 for Americans)&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>JazzKat1213</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
